  "answer": "This request has been filed before. PowerToys#46434 asks for CPU and GPU temperatures alongside the CPU, memory, network and GPU readings in the Command Palette Dock. There is no built-in way to do this yet, so please follow that issue and add a thumbs-up rather than opening a new one. According to the ticket, a contributor is working on a PR that adds a single thermal-zone temperature metric read through Windows performance counters (PDH). Windows has no native way to get exact per-component CPU or GPU temperatures. Those need vendor-specific drivers or WMI, so the first version may show only one general heat reading. In the meantime, you would need a third-party hardware monitor for detailed temperatures."
